WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
- So, what's up, Jamie?

00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:02.586
- Ted Lasso.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.796
- Oh, he's really gotten
up your bum, hasn't he?

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.924
- He's not even a real coach.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:12.095
- So, without further ado, the new manager
of AFC Richmond... Ted Lasso.

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:16.058
- Ted is a small-time American
football coach,

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:18.477
gets hired to coach
a professional soccer team in the UK.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.645
- Jesus.

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:22.439
- He doesn't know the rules
of football when he comes here,

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:24.733
but our favorite version
of an American character

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:26.735
is ignorant
with curiosity.

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:29.071
- Why don't we just jump right in?
Anybody got any questions?

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:31.657
Oh, yeah.
No, should've saw that coming.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.450
- For a TV show
about football,

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.536
which is obviously
very male-dominated,

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:38.413
we have two super-strong
female characters.

00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:39.706
- What is it you do again?

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.751
- I'm sort of famous for being
almost famous.

00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:44.169
- Maybe think of it as Plan B.

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:46.880
- Rebecca and Keeley, I think,
when you first meet them,

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:49.675
are very different women,
who you might think might not get along,

00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:53.011
and actually become
extraordinarily wonderful friends.

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:56.557
- It made me think of you.
It's strong and a bit prickly.

00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:01.895
- It's really funny, and it's
sort of secretly a little bit deep.

00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:03.772
But don't
tell anyone I said that.

00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:05.482
- I think people
will fall in love with Ted,

00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:07.776
and I think they'll like
the message that he's bringing,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.739
which is you don't necessarily
have to be an expert in everything,

00:01:12.823 --> 00:01:14.575
you don't have to pretend
you're something you're not.

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:18.120
You can just be you,
and you can be a success

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:20.789
by being kind
and gracious and thoughtful.

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:21.665
- How do you feel?

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.918
- Yeah, just-- Dunno, there's
so many new feelings. All right, yeah.

00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:26.378
- Kind of like getting
your first pube, right?

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:27.880
- Yeah-- What?

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:30.632
- Even if it's written in a way
where there's pure humor in it,

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:32.301
Ted is somebody
that would expand your mind

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:34.344
when you don't
realize it's happening.

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:36.513
- All the characters
who come across Ted

00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:39.183
are changed by him
in an amazing, heart-warming way.

00:01:39.266 --> 00:01:42.102
- I have a real tricky time hearing folks
who don't believe in themselves,

00:01:42.186 --> 00:01:44.897
so I'm gonna ask you real quick again:
Do you think this idea will work?

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.982
- Yeah, I do.
- Whoa!

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:50.277
Why are you screaming at us,
Nate? We're right here.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.740
- It's a genuinely funny show,
and if you've got 30 to 40 minutes,

00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:56.074
you're not gonna
regret watching it.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.577
- I don't think I can get away
with that anymore.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.704
- Sure, you could.
Fashion's all about confidence.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:01.872
You know,
if I didn't have any confidence,

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.707
I never would've
worn pajamas to my prom,

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.542
and ended up in jail
the rest of that night,

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:07.044
but you don't want to hear that story,
so I ain't gonna tell it.

